+## 3. Today's timeboxed execution
+
+Times are relative to starting this plan with the required operator decisions
+and a responsive supported runtime. They are work budgets and decision deadlines,
+not promises that the outstanding protocol or release will finish in eight hours.
+There is no automatic commit, push, infrastructure provisioning or native probe.
+
+| Elapsed | Owner and action | Observable output / stop rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0-30 min | Integration owner + release owner: pin the exact candidate and existing evidence; assign technical, QA, UX/evaluation and release accountability. Confirm the supported POSIX route. Obtain the current Linux child's artifact/run identity and actual result if available, without restarting an uncertain admitted run. | A usable execution route with artifact binding and an observable result channel. If absent, use the previously selected GitHub CI route only after separate commit/push authorization. Do not spend the day polling an unavailable child, infer success from idle notifications, or weaken Windows refusal. |
+| 0-60 min, parallel preparation | Release/QA owner: select the intended launch claim, review the open policy decisions, prepare native/campaign appointments and public-review material. Obtain each separately required authorization before execution. | Named decisions and evidence owners, not another blanket "proceed" interpreted as schema/cap/release approval. No external requests or PR publication without authorization. |
+| 30-120 min | Safety owner: work only on ownership-safe dependency recovery. Specify the current/before/owned-output identities and every race boundary; preflight every required blob before any restoration. Review the protocol before production changes. In parallel, starter owner reproduces absent-database rollback and stale-owner races on POSIX. | Distinguishing red controls and a reviewed correction, or a precise unresolved protocol decision. If human content can still be overwritten, release remains no-go; do not ship the previously rejected post-resolver-snapshot candidate. |
+| 60-180 min, parallel isolated work | Protocol integration owner: turn the partial 29-row candidate into an exact remaining-obligation map and resolve the blocked policy choices; identify the next end-to-end slice, not another helper-only success. Starter owner may finish independently specified repairs without touching shared kernel owners. | Explicit reviewed interfaces, capacity charges, missing rows and next acceptance trace. This timebox does not assume the whole candidate can be finished. No arbitrary cap increase or schema activation. |
+| 120-240 min | Integrate only reviewed, authorized corrections that pass focused real-process/Git/SQLite controls. Include the small lesson-retirement repair only if it cannot delay safety/protocol work. Run fast types/lints and affected checks at each coherent integration. | A coherent source candidate, full consumer wiring, unchanged safety assertions, and either approved measured limits or a passing fit. Reject unsafe/over-budget changes; retain their evidence separately. |
+| 240-360 min, if a safe candidate exists | QA validates one frozen artifact: complete `npm run ci` on supported POSIX, applicable Ubuntu/macOS jobs, Windows portability, built acceptance on Node 24 and minimum Node 22.12. Native observer runs only separately authorized probes on a pinned tuple. | Persist exit codes, totals including cancellations/skips, runtime/source/bundle/manifest identities, raw logs and independent dispositions. Native failures remain failures; CI is not host evidence. A failed gate returns to a bounded repair, then a new exact candidate. |
+| 360-480 min | Release owner reconciles the acceptance ledger, unresolved risks and Should decisions. If requested, perform staged and range privacy checks before commit/push, then verify exact-source hosted CI. Review the actual install/disable/recovery path before any evaluation distribution. | Publish an explicit go/no-go against the chosen claim. No valuable-data use while recovery is unsafe. No public R1 if any required gate is missing. Preserve a reviewable candidate even when the answer is no-go. |
